        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "VAIRA′GYAS′ATAKA.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 1. चूडोत्तंसित &c.—In this Sl. Hara is described as a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "lamp having for its flame the crescent moon, burning the moth",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "of Káma, and dispelling the darkness in the form of मोह. उत्तंसित",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "worn as a head-ornament. चञ्चन्ती-moving, quivering. लीलादग्ध०-",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "see Kum. III. 72. दशा-(1) a wick; (2) the condition of. प्राग्भार-",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "a mass or heap of; (an uncommon word; see Mál. Mád. V. 29.)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "उच्चाटयन्—removing, entirely dispelling. Cf. Nai. III. 7. विजयते—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "सर्वोत्कर्षेण वर्तते-shines pre-eminently. Fig. Rûpaka.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 2. The poet herein gives three causes of the decadence",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of learning—first, learned men themselves do not encourage it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "being jealous of new aspirants for literary honours; secondly,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "wealthy men in their own self-sufficiency despise knowledge;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "and lastly, ignorant men do not encourage it because they cannot",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "appreciate it. प्रभवः—the great, the rich. अबोधोपहताः—Lit. smit-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "ten by ignorance or want of understanding; incapable of appre-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "ciating merits. जीर्ण—p. p. of जॄ, absorbed; see infra. sl. 84",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "and cf. Mis. sl. 3.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl, 3. निधिशङ्कया—in the expectation of (finding) a treasure.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ध्माताः—fused, smelted. There may also be a reference to alchemy",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "here. धातवः—Metallic ores, minerals. मंत्राराधन—here means",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "securing the magical power with which some incantations are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "supposed to endow a man who repeats them according to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "rules or manner prescribed in the Tantras. श्मशाने—the cemetery",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "being the usual place for such practices. काण० &c.—a broken",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "cowrie shell. श्मशान—derived as शवाः शेरते अत्र; a comp. of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "पृषोदरादि class.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 4. देशं भ्रान्तम्—traversed (by me). The construction is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "peculiar. The subj. मया is understood. By the sûtra ‘गत्यर्थाकर्मक’—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Pán. III. 4. 12, त is added भावे to verbs implying motion",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "or used intransitively. देशं is an acc. of place. Mr. Telang cites",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "as a parallel instance ‘निजाश्रमपदं प्रति गतं च मुनिना’ Pra. II; Cf,",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
